---
import '~/assets/styles/tailwind.css';
import CommonMeta from '~/components/common/CommonMeta.astro';
import Metadata from '~/components/common/Metadata.astro';
import Favicons from '~/components/Favicons.astro';
import { getCanonical } from '~/utils/permalinks';
import ShapeLab from '~/components/joyan/ShapeLab.astro';
const metadata = {
  title: 'Shape and dither study',
  description: 'Isolated laboratory for the dot-scene engine: every cell mask, ramp, dither mode and cell geometry side by side.',
  canonical: String(getCanonical('/lab/shapes')),
  robots: { index: false, follow: false },
};
// The cost line is a prop so the page cannot claim a number nobody measured; the
// numbers below are the WU17 build measurements.
const cost = 'Measured cost, gzip level 6, the same engine chunk both laboratory routes share: 23366 B of JavaScript raw / 9508 B gzip for the engine, the scene, the shape catalogue and the runtime; the whole laboratory allowance is 34876 B gzip, capped at 36924 B (measured + 2048 B). The scene, the bake and the landing five chunks are unchanged by this unit.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr">
  <head>
    <CommonMeta />
    <Favicons />
    <Metadata {...metadata} lang="en" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0B0B0C" />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-ink-950 font-sans text-bone-100 antialiased">
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <a data-lab-return data-astro-reload href="/" class="font-mono text-sm text-bone-100 underline underline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-accent">← Return to landing</a>
    <header class="my-10">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-plomo-400">Lab / WU17 / experimental only</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl tracking-tight text-bone-50 sm:text-5xl">Shapes, not only dots.</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose text-bone-100">
        The dot is one mask among eleven. This laboratory puts the whole catalogue on the same scene, the same
        measured coverage ladder and the same palette, with the ramp, the dither mode, the cell geometry and the
        grid density switchable, and a fixed board that draws every shape at once.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm text-plomo-400">
        The other laboratory is the film and the library comparison:
        <a href="/lab/ascii" class="underline underline-offset-4">/lab/ascii</a>. Both are noindex, neither is a
        product surface, and neither changes the landing page.
      </p>
    </header>
    <ShapeLab scene="joyan-night-coast" cost={cost} />
    <footer class="border-t border-hairline pt-8 text-sm text-plomo-400">
      <p>The masks, the derivation of each size from the coverage ladder, the measured cost of each option and the
        pitch at which it stops reading are written up in <span class="font-mono">docs/MOTOR-ESCENAS.md</span>
        (Spanish) and <span class="font-mono">docs/DESIGN.md</span> (English). The measurements say what is
        comparable and what breaks down; which shape looks better is the reader's call.</p>
    </footer>
  </main>
  </body>
</html>
